<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 250 0 R
/T (From PC4 \(outside the private LAN\), pinging the public IP 172.40.0.5 results in 100% loss. Thisis expected, as NAT only translates outgoing traffic from the private PCs \(PC6-PC10\). The private PCs cannot be reached directly from outside. From PC6-PC10, pinging any address in the external network \(for example, Router0 or PC4 if routing allows\) succeeds, showing that PATis working and all five PCs share the public IP correctly )
/E (From PC4 \(outside the private LAN\), pinging the public IP 172.40.0.5 results in 100% loss. Thisis expected, as NAT only translates outgoing traffic from the private PCs \(PC6-PC10\). The private PCs cannot be reached directly from outside. From PC6-PC10, pinging any address in the external network \(for example, Router0 or PC4 if routing allows\) succeeds, showing that PATis working and all five PCs share the public IP correctly )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
